Both halves of #979 are now shipped. With --output-format stream-json, a run that really restored a saved session now prints {"type":"sessionRestored","messages":N} directly after the first agentStart line. Build, tests (all 18 test binaries), clippy and fmt pass. It's committed as 3c2c3591, and I commented on #979 with the exact line and closed it.

When the line appears:
• **When:** once per process, only if --continue or --continue-strict actually restored a session. N is the count of restored messages.
• **When it's absent:** no `--continue` flag, or a plain `--continue` whose restore failed. A failed restore never prints `messages: 0`, which would look like an empty session was restored.
• **Other modes:** text, json and --print output are unchanged, and so is a stream-json run without --continue.

How it's built:
• **New `src/prompt/stream_session_restored.rs:** the stream-json writer now goes through this module. On a successful restore, main.rs records the message count once; the writer prints the line after the first agentStart` and then clears it, so later turns don't repeat it.
• **Key order:** the line is built by hand because the JSON library sorts keys and would have put messages before type. That broke my first version of the test.

Tests:
• **Unit tests, writing into a buffer:** the line's exact text and position after `agentStart`; output identical to before when nothing was restored; no repeat on a second turn; only agentStart triggers it.
• **Two tests in tests/print_stdout_contract.rs that run the real binary:** the saved session they load comes from a real `--save-session` run, not hand-written JSON. They check both `--continue` and `--continue-strict`, a run with no --continue, and a failed plain --continue.
• **Positive control (break → run → restore in one command):** with the emission disabled, the four tests that expect the line failed by name. The tests that expect no line still passed. The file was restored and no `NEUTERED` marker is left.

Docs: the line, its exact shape and when it's absent are in docs/src/usage/piped-mode.md and docs/src/features/sessions.md. I also added a short entry next to the src/main.rs bullet in ARCHITECTURE.md.
